-- title:
--   Node values as a product of branch norms
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a level $N \neq 0$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ with a ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$, modular polynomial data `data` for $q$ whose bivariate reduction modulo $q$ equals $(\mathrm{C}X^{q}-X)(\mathrm{C}X-X^{q})$ (`hKr`), integrality `hα`, `hβ` of the two degeneracy maps from level $N$ to level $Nq$, a place specialisation $P$ and a prolongation tuple $R$ over it, with $k$ perfect. Let $K \subset \overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$, $w$ a place of $\operatorname{modularFunctionFieldC} k\,N$, $c$ a pair of node coordinates $x,y$ at $w$, and write $B := R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\,K\,w$ for the ring of functions in $\operatorname{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ integral for $R.R_1$, for $R.R_2$ and for every place $V$ over the algebraic closure with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V = w$, whose Laurent expansion lies in $\mathrm{NodeLocalized.fieldOver}\,(Nq)\,K$, and $\mathcal O := A \cap K$ for the coefficient subring, embedded in $B$ as constants by $R.\mathrm{nodeConst}$. Assume: $\varpi \in \mathcal O$ is nonzero; $B$ is local and Noetherian with maximal ideal $(\mathrm{nodeConst}\,\varpi, x, y)$; every element of $B$ differs from some constant by a non-unit (`hres`); the value integrality law, namely $V.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f \in A$ for $f$ in the node integers and $V$ over $w$; $w$ is a supersingular place (rational, affine geometric, with supersingular $j$-value); $W$ is a complete discrete valuation domain with irreducible $\pi$, $E \geq 1$, and $\iota$ is a ring isomorphism from the $\mathfrak m_B$-adic completion of $B$ to the crossing model $\mathcal R := \mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2, W)/(X_0X_1 - \pi^{E})$ with $\iota(\varpi) = \mathrm{const}\,\pi$ and $\iota(x) = U \cdot \alpha_U$ for a unit $\alpha_U$; every prime strictly below a non-maximal prime of $B$ is $\bot$ (`hht`); every element of $\mathrm{NodeLocalized.fieldOver}\,(Nq)\,K$ is a ratio of two elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator (`hfrac`); $\mathcal O$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal $(\varpi)$ and $\tau$ is an isomorphism from its adic completion to $W$ matching $\iota$ on constants and sending $\varpi$ to $\pi$; $\mathfrak q$ is a nonzero prime of $B$ containing no nonzero constant; $j$ is a ring homomorphism from the adic completion of $\mathcal O$ to the valuation integers of the completion $C$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ for the valuation of $A$, compatible with the inclusion $\mathcal O \subset \overline{\mathbb Q} \to C$. Finally let $g \in B$ and let $S$ be a finite set of places of $\operatorname{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ consisting exactly of those $V$ with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V = w$ whose evaluation kernel on $B$ is precisely $\mathfrak q$, and assume that $\#S$, as an element of $\mathbb N_\infty$, equals the sum of the $W$-ranks of $\mathcal R/Q$ over the primes $Q$ of $\mathcal R$ that are minimal over the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak q$ under $\iota$ and do not contain $\mathrm{const}\,\pi$. The conclusion is that in $C$ the image of $\prod_{V \in S} V.\mathrm{evalAt}\,g$ equals the image under $j \circ \tau^{-1}$ of the product, over those same primes $Q$, of the norms $\mathrm{Algebra.norm}\,W$ of the class of $\iota(g)$ in $\mathcal R/Q$.
--
--   This is the multiplicative companion of the per-kernel count of places above a supersingular node of $X_0(Nq)$: the values at the places with evaluation kernel $\mathfrak q$ are grouped, branch by branch, into norms computed on the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^{E})$. It is used in the derivation of the factorisation of $\prod_{V \in S} V.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the second node coordinate as a power of a uniformiser times units.
